==Gameplay==
{{#ifeq:{{{Gameplay|}}}||The MJS 1000 is a balanced Diesel Engine included with the Baseset for the Sub-Artic and Sub-Tropical climates. It has good power and speed, which make it a viable option for both cargo and passenger lines. Its maximum speed of 104 km/h make it so this engine can share lines with the Kelling 3100 for Mixed Traffic Lines.

It can pull a fully loaded 7 tile long freight train without hindering its acceleration, speed or climbing ability.|{{{Gameplay}}}}}

==Trivia==
{{#ifeq:{{{Trivia|}}}||*The MJS 1000 likely draws inspiration from many diesel locomotives, both for its statistics and appearance, such as the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ALCO_RS-3 ALCO RS-3], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ALCO_RS-11 ALCO RS-11], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ALCO_Century_425 ALCO Century 425] and the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ALCO_MRS-1 ALCO MRS-1] (From which it might have drawn inspiration for its name). All these engines were built and ran across North America in the midst and second half of the 20th Century.

*The updated sprite for the MJS 1000 gives it an appearance more in line with the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SNCF_Class_BB_66000 SNFC Class BB 66000] and other [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Center-cab_locomotives Center-cab Locomotives].

*Given its capabilities, and similarly to its real-life counterparts, it could be said that the MJS1000 fulfills the role of a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_switcher_locomotive Road Switcher Locomotive]

*The MJS1000 competes directly with the CS2400 for the role of a Road Switcher; with the MJS1000 having a longer lifespan while the CS2400 is cheaper and stronger. This reflects the historic and ongoing [https://unotechengineering.com/emd-vs-alco-vs-ge/ rivalry between ALCO and EMD]|{{{Trivia}}}}}

